WEBVTT

00:00.375 --> 00:05.574
Yume toki ashita no koto wa

00:05.848 --> 00:11.377
Dareni mo mienu deshou

00:13.255 --> 00:18.716
Me o tojite kimi o omou

00:19.394 --> 00:25.196
Itsuka de au

00:25.534 --> 00:31.734
Kaze no hana yo, Saa hiraku no yo

00:32.007 --> 00:38.412
Watashi no kono me ni haru o misete

00:38.714 --> 00:44.812
Kaze no hana yo, Saa hiraku no yo

00:45.087 --> 00:51.219
Sayonara fuyu no machi

00:51.593 --> 00:58.055
Kaze no hana yo, Saa hiraku no yo

00:58.333 --> 01:04.829
Watashi no kokoro ni haru o yonde

01:04.973 --> 01:11.105
Kaze no hana yo, Saa hiraku no yo

01:11.413 --> 01:17.875
Sayonara yukitachi yo

01:40.609 --> 01:44.279
So when the certification exam or
whatever is over, you'll come home?

01:44.279 --> 01:50.052
Yeah. Oyamada-sensei will assign
a task for me to use my Special Power.

01:50.052 --> 01:52.254
Hey, can I eat
this sweet roll?

01:52.254 --> 01:55.123
Hush, Haru. I'm on the phone
with Yume right now.

01:55.123 --> 01:58.260
What? In Tokyo?
I wanna talk to her, too!

01:58.260 --> 02:00.162
Educational Psychology
- Oh, come on, Haru!

02:00.162 --> 02:01.496
Educational Psychology
- Oh, come on, Haru!
- Give it to me, Big Sis!

02:01.496 --> 02:03.632
Yume, ya' doin' okay?

02:03.632 --> 02:06.032
Hey, Haru!
Yep, I'm just fine.

02:06.568 --> 02:09.004
Is the certification exam hard?

02:09.004 --> 02:12.307
Middle East Cease
Fire Agreement Reached.
It's a piece of cake.
I'm smart.

02:12.307 --> 02:16.745
I was even praised by
a superior officer, like a Councilor.

02:16.745 --> 02:18.975
I'm fine. I'm just fine.

02:20.983 --> 02:25.818
United Nations Mage Cease-Fire
Arbitration Committee A Success

02:27.055 --> 02:28.991
Hello, Yume?

02:28.991 --> 02:33.485
What?
Um, yeah, I'm listening.

02:34.897 --> 02:40.563
Hey, Aya?
I'm glad I was born a mage.

02:41.370 --> 02:46.137
I want to become a great mage
soon and be useful to people.

02:47.843 --> 02:52.439
"The Destination of Special Power"

02:58.887 --> 03:01.253
The Takahashis

03:17.940 --> 03:21.535
This is my mother.
Her name is Takahashi Mitsuko.

03:22.544 --> 03:25.843
Thank you in advance
for your help.

03:28.550 --> 03:31.075
Well then, please begin.

03:31.153 --> 03:37.025
Yes. As I've already explained,
Kikuchi here will use her Special Power.

03:37.025 --> 03:41.655
Thank you for your trust.
I'm Kikuchi Yume.

03:44.900 --> 03:49.171
I will now use Special Power
to revert this house,

03:49.171 --> 03:52.368
until noon, to its condition
50 years ago...

04:01.383 --> 04:03.510
"With all my precious feelings
in my heart..."

04:37.285 --> 04:39.480
Whoa! This is amazing!

04:39.688 --> 04:41.656
How do you like it, Mother?

04:45.293 --> 04:48.626
If you'd like,
I'll show you the other rooms.

05:28.870 --> 05:31.202
You like it here best,
don't you?

05:31.807 --> 05:33.001
Yes.

05:33.542 --> 05:36.136
Shall I cook something for you?

05:39.181 --> 05:42.344
She wants to do it herself.

05:42.651 --> 05:44.619
Oh, excuse me. I...

05:45.420 --> 05:47.888
Really, I'm sorry.

05:50.258 --> 05:52.852
I'd like to reverse
Mitsuko-san's time, also.

05:53.395 --> 05:54.862
What do you mean?

05:56.198 --> 05:58.867
If her body were as strong
as it used to be,

05:58.867 --> 06:00.596
she could work easier...

06:00.769 --> 06:01.599
Yume-chan...

06:01.770 --> 06:02.702
Yes.

06:04.706 --> 06:09.377
"Use of Special Power
to interfere with life itself,

06:09.377 --> 06:14.049
vital organs or tissues,
is strictly prohibited."

06:14.049 --> 06:15.217
Yes.

06:15.217 --> 06:18.053
It is a type of Special Power
you should not use lightly.

06:18.053 --> 06:21.723
Yes. I apologize.

06:21.723 --> 06:23.122
Huh?

06:25.293 --> 06:26.590
Oyamada-sensei?

06:27.696 --> 06:30.460
Never mind.
Shall we go back?

06:31.166 --> 06:32.155
Yes.

06:38.206 --> 06:40.470
The Takahashis

06:49.017 --> 06:53.716
My mother said that she'd move
to an assisted living facility.

06:54.756 --> 06:56.587
She has a sharp mind,
doesn't she?

06:56.958 --> 07:01.520
Since my father died, I've been
taking care of my mother.

07:01.763 --> 07:04.630
And I think nothing of it...

07:04.900 --> 07:09.599
She says my life will be wasted
if she stays with me much longer.

07:13.275 --> 07:16.176
She's still attached, of course.

07:16.444 --> 07:19.902
She asked that this house be
returned to its original condition.

07:20.615 --> 07:25.575
Once she sets her mind on something,
she won't budge. She's very stubborn.

07:25.620 --> 07:28.453
Um... My Grandmother
is stubborn, too.

07:29.624 --> 07:31.285
Really? Is she well?

07:31.626 --> 07:33.389
Yes, thank goodness.

07:33.795 --> 07:35.285
Good.

07:35.730 --> 07:39.791
Thank you for your
heartfelt mage action.

07:59.921 --> 08:01.855
We'll be leaving now.

08:04.059 --> 08:05.093
What?

08:05.093 --> 08:06.560
Nothing.

08:09.698 --> 08:11.928
Well then, excuse me...

08:12.434 --> 08:14.425
I regret making the request.

08:26.681 --> 08:30.310
So, my mage action
was wrong, wasn't it?

08:30.685 --> 08:34.086
No. It was very well done
in compliance with the request.

08:34.522 --> 08:35.853
But Mitsuko-san...

08:36.057 --> 08:37.859
After you complete
your mage action,

08:37.859 --> 08:40.629
don't let your heart
linger with the applicant.

08:40.629 --> 08:42.197
What?

08:42.197 --> 08:44.529
The task was
successfully completed.

09:35.417 --> 09:37.248
Zennosuke quit.

09:37.585 --> 09:41.489
I knew it. Did he go back
to the soccer club?

09:41.489 --> 09:42.490
What?

09:42.490 --> 09:47.359
Oh, nothing. Do you know where
Zennosuke-san goes to high school?

09:47.562 --> 09:50.531
Tokyo Prefecture
Kitazawa Public High School

09:52.600 --> 09:54.830
Zennosuke?
Why would he be here?

09:55.603 --> 09:56.661
But...

09:57.005 --> 10:00.270
He can't move his leg.
What would he come here for?

10:00.508 --> 10:04.569
Then Zennosuke-san hasn't
come back even once?

10:04.679 --> 10:07.375
That's right.
You don't give up.

10:07.749 --> 10:10.185
He's gotta be playing
around somewhere!

10:10.185 --> 10:11.953
- Uh... wait...
- All right!

10:11.953 --> 10:15.013
Next we split into offense and
defense to test the formation...

10:19.627 --> 10:21.296
Thank you for
riding with us today.

10:21.296 --> 10:23.465
To ensure a pleasant
trip for all passengers,

10:23.465 --> 10:25.956
please turn off your cell phones
on the train. Thank you.

10:41.015 --> 10:45.286
Welcome to
our shopping district.

10:45.286 --> 10:48.656
Thank you for
your patronage here today.

10:48.656 --> 10:52.994
We hope you'll have a pleasant
shopping experience...

10:52.994 --> 10:56.327
Welcome! Ah, are you the mage
from the other day?

10:57.298 --> 11:01.359
Um... The glass at the bakery
and the clock shop...

11:01.503 --> 11:03.835
did they turn back
to the way they were?

11:04.005 --> 11:07.308
No, that's not it.
They got damaged again.

11:07.308 --> 11:09.503
My shutters are
completely trashed, too.

11:09.744 --> 11:11.012
Oh, no.

11:11.012 --> 11:14.778
Even though you did a great job,
it's still a cat-and-mouse game.

11:15.016 --> 11:16.584
A cat-and-mouse game...

11:16.584 --> 11:20.645
I guess mage actions don't provide
the fundamental solutions to problems.

11:21.990 --> 11:23.821
Ah! Welcome!

11:26.761 --> 11:30.197
Odakyu Line
Shimo-Kitazawa Station

11:32.100 --> 11:34.330
Shimo-Kitazawa
Shopping Street

11:35.170 --> 11:36.364
Hey, Yume!

11:36.571 --> 11:38.539
What's wrong?
Did something happen?

11:38.973 --> 11:40.167
It's nothing.

11:40.642 --> 11:44.510
You look horrible. Did you
lose your smile somewhere?

11:44.712 --> 11:47.449
Yume-san, you have wrinkles
between your eyes.

11:47.449 --> 11:48.716
So what?

11:48.716 --> 11:52.153
Hey, Yume. Since
you're going home soon,

11:52.153 --> 11:56.057
we were talking about throwing
a farewell party for you.

11:56.057 --> 11:57.649
I don't want one.

11:58.159 --> 12:00.787
Don't be bashful,
Master Mage!

12:01.963 --> 12:08.994
I'm not a master mage!
My Special Power is...

12:34.662 --> 12:36.664
Kikuchi Yume-san
is exceptional.

12:36.664 --> 12:39.133
Bureau of Mage Labor Mage
Trainee Resume: Kikuchi Yume
She didn't make any major mistakes.

12:39.133 --> 12:42.660
Bureau of Mage Labor Mage
Trainee Resume: Kikuchi Yume
And she is extremely compassionate
when she uses her Special Power.

12:44.672 --> 12:47.607
I'm planning on giving her the
certification exam this coming weekend.

12:48.276 --> 12:49.573
I understand.

12:50.111 --> 12:51.578
Then, if you'll excuse me...

12:52.680 --> 12:54.048
Oyamada Masami-san?

12:54.048 --> 12:55.149
Yes.

12:55.149 --> 13:00.883
How long do you plan on using your
Special Power to punish yourself?

13:01.789 --> 13:05.782
With all due respect, I have not used
my Special Power wrongfully.

13:07.295 --> 13:11.254
Is that what SHE wished?

13:13.868 --> 13:15.233
Excuse me.

13:36.157 --> 13:39.558
Unless you talk to us,
we can't understand you.

13:40.094 --> 13:44.121
That's fine.
This is my problem.

13:44.532 --> 13:49.026
But maybe we can be there for you.
Actually we want to be there for you!

13:50.104 --> 13:52.698
It's no use talking to non-mages...

13:52.840 --> 13:54.175
What's that?

13:54.175 --> 13:57.845
Are you saying that only the honorable
mages can understand your problem?

13:57.845 --> 14:00.075
If it's not Masami-chan,
then it won't work?

14:01.015 --> 14:03.347
I'm not saying that at all.

14:04.552 --> 14:06.144
Please leave me alone.

14:23.171 --> 14:26.231
Unbelievable. Everyone's so
caught up in their own problems.

14:26.674 --> 14:28.642
You've got no room
to talk, Milinda-san.

14:28.876 --> 14:30.400
What? Me?

14:31.212 --> 14:34.704
Is it right to keep things
going with Boss this way?

14:34.749 --> 14:39.015
No, it's not right. That's why
I've been working hard on him.

14:39.554 --> 14:42.717
Yeah, right.
All I see is a joke.

14:43.157 --> 14:45.853
You really want me to
seduce him in front of you?

14:46.894 --> 14:48.794
You're in the same situation
I was a while back.

14:48.863 --> 14:49.955
What do you mean?

14:54.836 --> 14:58.067
You're afraid of
finding the answer.

15:01.209 --> 15:03.700
Are you fine...
with things the way they are?

15:15.923 --> 15:18.619
I have a little headache.
I'm going to bed.

15:18.793 --> 15:20.094
Are you all right?

15:20.094 --> 15:21.083
I'm fine.

15:21.696 --> 15:25.188
Then, if you need anything,
let me know right away.

15:25.533 --> 15:26.591
Yes.

15:27.935 --> 15:30.267
As for...
the certification exam...

15:31.539 --> 15:32.597
Yes...

15:33.441 --> 15:36.274
As scheduled,
it will be given this weekend.

15:36.878 --> 15:37.867
Yes.

15:38.846 --> 15:40.279
All right, then.

16:15.983 --> 16:23.480
Is that so? Yes.
I understand. Yes. Bye.

16:24.826 --> 16:26.418
Did something happen?

16:30.331 --> 16:31.365
Sensei?

16:31.365 --> 16:33.993
I just got a call from
the Bureau of Mage Labor.

16:34.569 --> 16:36.969
Takahashi-san's house
is on fire, they said.

16:37.371 --> 16:39.339
They also said the cause
of the fire is suspicious.

16:39.807 --> 16:40.933
What do you mean?

16:42.577 --> 16:45.603
It's possible that it was started
by a family member.

16:46.247 --> 16:48.841
There weren't any flaws
in our mage action?

16:52.286 --> 16:53.844
Caused by a family member?

16:54.355 --> 16:56.016
It's a possibility...

17:09.036 --> 17:10.738
Ouch!

17:10.738 --> 17:14.442
What are you doing?
Don't go out to watch the fire!

17:14.442 --> 17:17.578
You're not a rubberneck,
so don't do it.

17:17.578 --> 17:19.914
Look...
Your elbow's bleeding.

17:19.914 --> 17:21.245
I'm fine.

17:22.583 --> 17:24.986
But you're bleeding.

17:24.986 --> 17:29.389
It's fine. It's my little scratch,
so it doesn't matter!

17:29.657 --> 17:30.749
Yume...

17:32.593 --> 17:33.992
What happened?

17:38.099 --> 17:41.364
You won't answer
my question, as usual...

17:55.249 --> 17:57.418
- Are there still people inside?

17:57.418 --> 17:58.885
- Are there still people inside?
- How did it start?

18:03.257 --> 18:06.021
It's going to burn
to the ground!

18:25.112 --> 18:27.410
Excuse me!
Let me through!

18:28.049 --> 18:31.177
Step back!
It's dangerous! Step back!

18:31.819 --> 18:35.255
Takahashi-san!
Mitsuko-san! Kazuo-san!

18:36.691 --> 18:38.454
- Oh!
- Ah!

18:44.398 --> 18:46.133
Unbelievable!

18:46.133 --> 18:47.468
Ah! Look out!

18:47.468 --> 18:49.459
- There it goes!
- Oh, my gosh!

18:56.978 --> 18:58.809
Stop your mage action!

18:59.647 --> 19:00.978
Sensei...

19:01.482 --> 19:04.252
The Takahashis have
been taken to the hospital.

19:04.252 --> 19:05.480
What?

19:10.324 --> 19:11.848
Hey! Get away!

19:14.595 --> 19:17.462
Stop your mage action.

19:27.842 --> 19:31.903
Mitsuko-san said,
"I regret making the request."

19:32.980 --> 19:35.349
My mage action
must have been wrong.

19:35.349 --> 19:37.184
That's not the case.

19:37.184 --> 19:39.921
I must have done
something wrong.

19:39.921 --> 19:41.855
Yume-chan, that's not true.

19:42.790 --> 19:45.987
No one can understand
Mitsuko-san's feelings.

19:50.131 --> 19:53.794
Once a mage action is completed,
please forget about the applicant.

19:53.868 --> 19:55.335
I can't!

19:56.504 --> 19:59.200
That's too... cold!

19:59.273 --> 20:01.104
Sensei, you're cold!

20:04.545 --> 20:05.534
Yume-chan!

20:14.221 --> 20:15.890
Where are you going?

20:15.890 --> 20:18.256
To the hospital that
admitted the Takahashis.

20:19.393 --> 20:20.553
Which hospital?

20:24.165 --> 20:27.657
What in the world
have I been doing?

20:28.502 --> 20:31.906
I used my Special Power
because I wanted her to get better...

20:31.906 --> 20:36.070
because I wanted her
to be happy...

20:38.079 --> 20:41.139
You cannot step into
someone else's heart...

20:46.253 --> 20:49.586
Mages use Special Power
as requested.

20:50.324 --> 20:53.020
That's the way of life
for a mage...

20:58.299 --> 21:00.859
That's so... lonesome.

21:03.604 --> 21:06.437
If so, then what is
Special Power?

21:08.275 --> 21:11.608
Why does such
a thing even exist?

21:20.287 --> 21:26.851
Furikaereba ima demo soko ni

21:29.630 --> 21:36.263
Oikaketeta mirai ga atta

21:37.972 --> 21:47.108
Boku no kokoro ni aru taisetsu na mono

21:47.214 --> 21:52.049
Mada mienai ao to

21:53.120 --> 21:59.821
Nagareru kumo ni negatta

22:02.730 --> 22:04.823
Under the Blue Sky

22:05.099 --> 22:11.868
Ano hi bokura ga egaita yume kara

22:12.139 --> 22:18.908
Samenai you ni tomaranai you ni

22:21.682 --> 22:23.616
Under the Blue Sky

22:23.818 --> 22:30.519
Kagayaki nagara aruiteikou yo

22:31.058 --> 22:37.019
Owaranai tabi wa tsuzuku

22:49.710 --> 22:51.812
PREVIEW

22:51.812 --> 22:56.884
When you passed away, my heart
shattered into a thousand pieces...

22:56.884 --> 23:02.720
When you passed away,
my future stopped shining...

23:03.057 --> 23:07.561
Grief... Sorrow... Despair...

23:07.561 --> 23:11.198
I ran out of tears...

23:11.198 --> 23:14.429
And what remained with me was...

23:15.736 --> 23:19.604
"A Broken Rainbow"
Episode Eleven is "A Broken Rainbow."
